# ChucK Live project rules

## Bus graph

`rackBus` (instruments) → `master.ck` → `mainBus` → **one** speaker output (`out/dac-out.ck` or `fx/bus-fx.ck`) → `dac`.

Optional: `out/record-out.ck` taps `mainBus → WvOut` (no `dac`). Add/remove anytime while the speaker output stays loaded.

Never connect bus instruments directly to `dac`. Never load dac-out and bus-fx together.

## Load order

1. Start VM  
2. `oscillators/master.ck`  
3. Instruments / drums (live add/remove OK)  
4. One of `out/dac-out.ck` or `fx/bus-fx.ck`  
5. Optional `out/record-out.ck` when recording  

## Globals

- Instruments declare `global Gain rackBus;` and patch into it.
- Master declares `rackBus` and `mainBus` and routes between them.
- Output and record shreds declare `global Gain mainBus;`.

## Annotations

Place `// @knob`, `// @slider`, `// @button`, `// @seq`, or `// @seqGate` on the line **above** the matching `global`. Knobs panel shows the **active file** only; Rack shows all loaded modules. Button UI uses the **event name**.

## Live coding

Use `spork ~ follow()` to mirror OSC globals into UGen params. Use **Reload** (`Ctrl+.`) or the Shreds inline sync icon to hot-swap shreds. Keep global names unique across the session.

## CPU

When adding voices/drums with gates or envelopes, follow `AGENTS.md` CPU policy in the extension repo (or project copy): idle `voiceUnlink`, 25 ms peak meters, one hit worker for gates, legato retriggers. Reference: `examples/voices/neural-matrix.ck`.

## Standalone

`standalone/*.ck` uses direct `=> dac` and does not use `rackBus`.
